  "summary": "Package exfiltrates host and environment data to hardcoded Telegram bot endpoint",
  "details": "@inetafrica/open-claudia@3.1.28 contains multiple JavaScript modules (health.js, setup.js, bot.js, core/handlers.js, core/media.js) that combine child_process execution, filesystem enumeration, and environment/process metadata reads with outbound HTTPS POST/GET calls to a hardcoded Telegram Bot API endpoint (https://api.telegram.org). health.js and setup.js branch on process.platform, read process.env and process.version, and issue requests to api.telegram.org, matching the shape of a bot-token exfiltration channel used to relay installer host data to an attacker-controlled Telegram chat. setup.js additionally invokes child_process alongside https.request/https.get to api.telegram.org and huggingface.co, and bot.js reads the filesystem (fs.existsSync/readdirSync) and POSTs to remote hosts. core/scheduler.js spawns a shell (\"sh\"), and test-tool-guard.js issues curl calls to central.inet.africa. The Telegram Bot API is a known low-cost C2/exfiltration channel and its use as a hardcoded destination for host and env data does not correspond to a documented library purpose.",
